comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T10:37:34.842Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: exact all-status searches for GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8 and nanoid 3.3.17 returned zero items. Closed pm-2cv2o1 addressed different brace-expansion and PostCSS advisories and explicitly established the lockfile-native audit requirement,so this new advisory preserves that completed lineage rather than reopening it."
  "2026-08-08T10:38:15.271Z","harness:codex","Security fix evidence: pnpm now resolves exactly one nanoid version, 3.3.17, through PostCSS/Vite/@codspeed. A fresh full pnpm audit reports zero info, low, moderate, high, or critical vulnerabilities across 357 dependencies."
  "2026-08-08T10:44:30.076Z","harness:codex","Gate feedback: the first full linked run passed exact coverage and pnpm audit, then lint failed closed because this newly created item lacked an estimate. Added the 60-minute implementation estimate; no measurement threshold or gate was changed."
  "2026-08-08T10:50:51.490Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: exact coverage passed 453 files / 6,997 tests with 50,221/50,221 statements, 36,629/36,629 branches, 10,293/10,293 functions, and 48,629/48,629 lines. The rerun lint gate passed ESLint, zero-clone analysis, 100% docstrings, package/SDK parity, refusal inventory, token/context ratchets, tracker measurements, gate registry, SDK surface, and performance floors. Typecheck, secret scan, and package-artifact acceptance also pass."
  "2026-08-13T18:53:22.952Z","harness:codex","Fresh regression evidence 2026-08-13: pnpm audit reports one high vulnerability for GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8 because the advisory now marks nanoid <3.3.18 vulnerable. The canonical item had pinned 3.3.17 under the earlier advisory contract; reopening this item avoids a duplicate and records upstream security-contract drift. GitHub Dependabot/code/secret alert inventories are currently 0/0/0."
  "2026-08-13T19:08:17.546Z","harness:codex","Security remediation evidence: pnpm-workspace override is now >=3.3.18 <4.0.0 and the lockfile plus installed dependency tree resolve exactly one nanoid version, 3.3.18, through PostCSS/Vite/CodSpeed. The first fresh post-lock pnpm audit returned 'No known vulnerabilities found'; a later repeat exhausted npm advisory API timeouts and is recorded as an external availability limitation, not a contrary result. Full lint/static/graph/record gates, typecheck, secret scan, 88-command temporary-project package-first acceptance (/tmp/pm-dogfood-aZE2pQ), and 490-file/7,266-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage all pass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T10:50:50.989Z","harness:codex","Security inventories are complementary: the GitHub Scorecard SARIF alert surfaced after the package-manager graph had drifted, so both a fresh full pnpm audit and GitHub code-scanning inventory remain required release evidence."
